1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,111
Two friends pull a cart.

2
00:00:02,111 --> 00:00:03,867
A swimmer crosses a river.

3
00:00:03,867 --> 00:00:06,268
The wind and a string pull one kite.

4
00:00:06,668 --> 00:00:08,159
Two pulls act together.

5
00:00:08,159 --> 00:00:11,024
And the answer is not
just one plus the other.

6
00:00:11,474 --> 00:00:15,862
Aarav rides three kilometres east,
then four north, to reach college.

7
00:00:16,212 --> 00:00:18,042
His trip meter says seven.

8
00:00:18,042 --> 00:00:21,040
But college is only five
kilometres from home.

9
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:25,453
By the end of this video, that
strange sum will make perfect sense.

10
00:00:26,103 --> 00:00:27,962
So how do you add two vectors?

11
00:00:28,312 --> 00:00:30,005
Numbers add in a line.

12
00:00:30,005 --> 00:00:32,848
Three kilograms plus four is always seven.

13
00:00:33,248 --> 00:00:36,662
Vectors have a direction,
so we add them as arrows.

14
00:00:36,662 --> 00:00:38,418
This is the triangle law.

15
00:00:38,818 --> 00:00:40,261
Draw the first arrow.

16
00:00:40,261 --> 00:00:42,529
Start the second arrow at its head.

17
00:00:42,529 --> 00:00:43,541
Head to tail.

18
00:00:43,941 --> 00:00:47,572
The resultant runs from the
first tail to the last head.

19
00:00:47,572 --> 00:00:50,049
One arrow that does the job of both.

20
00:00:50,699 --> 00:00:53,654
Let's ride Aarav's route
on our motion notebook.

21
00:00:54,004 --> 00:00:55,618
Three kilometres east.

22
00:00:55,618 --> 00:00:57,033
That is vector A.

23
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:59,246
Then four kilometres north.

24
00:00:59,246 --> 00:01:02,034
That is vector B, starting where A ends.

25
00:01:02,434 --> 00:01:03,845
Slow motion replay.

26
00:01:03,845 --> 00:01:06,258
Watch the straight arrow from home.

27
00:01:06,258 --> 00:01:09,561
At college, this resultant
R is five kilometres.

28
00:01:10,061 --> 00:01:13,017
Now keep both lengths,
and change only the angle.

29
00:01:13,417 --> 00:01:15,030
Same direction: seven.

30
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:16,604
A right angle: five.

31
00:01:16,604 --> 00:01:18,673
Opposite directions: just one.

32
00:01:19,173 --> 00:01:20,485
The graph shows it.

33
00:01:20,485 --> 00:01:23,383
The resultant always stays
between one and seven.

34
00:01:24,033 --> 00:01:27,368
Now the size of R for any
angle, in small steps.

35
00:01:27,718 --> 00:01:28,618
Step one.

36
00:01:28,567 --> 00:01:31,785
Put B at the head of A, at an angle theta.

37
00:01:31,785 --> 00:01:33,607
Part of B lies along A.

38
00:01:33,607 --> 00:01:35,687
That part is B cosine theta.

39
00:01:36,437 --> 00:01:37,337
Step two.

40
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:39,747
The rest of B points straight across.

41
00:01:39,747 --> 00:01:41,640
That part is B sine theta.

42
00:01:42,390 --> 00:01:43,321
Step three.

43
00:01:43,321 --> 00:01:46,096
R is the long side of a right triangle.

44
00:01:46,096 --> 00:01:50,734
So R squared is the along part
squared, plus the across part squared.

45
00:01:51,484 --> 00:01:52,437
Step four.

46
00:01:52,437 --> 00:01:55,360
Sine squared plus cosine squared is one.

47
00:01:55,360 --> 00:02:00,506
So R squared equals A squared plus
B squared plus two AB cosine theta.

48
00:02:01,256 --> 00:02:02,156
Check it.

49
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,955
Zero degrees gives seven.

50
00:02:03,955 --> 00:02:05,357
Ninety gives five.

51
00:02:05,357 --> 00:02:06,980
One eighty gives one.

52
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:08,687
Remember this.

53
00:02:08,687 --> 00:02:13,362
Vectors add head to tail, and the
angle between them decides the answer.

54
00:02:14,062 --> 00:02:16,454
There is a second way
to draw the same sum.

55
00:02:16,804 --> 00:02:21,008
Or put both arrows tail to tail,
and complete a parallelogram.

56
00:02:21,008 --> 00:02:23,105
Its diagonal is the resultant.

57
00:02:23,505 --> 00:02:25,472
A then B, or B then A.

58
00:02:25,472 --> 00:02:27,469
Both reach the same corner.

59
00:02:27,469 --> 00:02:29,709
So A plus B equals B plus A.

60
00:02:30,109 --> 00:02:34,139
Add a vector to its exact opposite,
and you are back at the start: the

61
00:02:34,139 --> 00:02:35,916
zero vector, or null vector.

62
00:02:36,566 --> 00:02:37,829
Now subtraction.

63
00:02:37,829 --> 00:02:39,396
What is A minus B?

64
00:02:39,746 --> 00:02:43,812
Minus B is the same arrow as
B, pointing the opposite way.

65
00:02:44,212 --> 00:02:47,023
So A minus B is just A plus minus B.

66
00:02:47,023 --> 00:02:49,431
Flip B, then add head to tail.

67
00:02:49,831 --> 00:02:51,855
Same rule, one extra step.

68
00:02:52,455 --> 00:02:53,579
Side by side.

69
00:02:53,579 --> 00:02:57,325
Three east plus four north
gives five, north of east.

70
00:02:57,725 --> 00:03:01,277
Subtracting: flip four north
into four south, then add.

71
00:03:01,277 --> 00:03:03,376
Still five, but south of east.

72
00:03:03,976 --> 00:03:05,043
Now you try.

73
00:03:05,043 --> 00:03:08,785
Forces of three newtons and
four newtons act on a box.

74
00:03:08,785 --> 00:03:11,230
Can the resultant be eight newtons?

75
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:12,557
Pause and decide.

76
00:03:15,757 --> 00:03:16,657
No!

77
00:03:16,182 --> 00:03:19,275
The most is seven, when
both point the same way.

78
00:03:19,275 --> 00:03:22,314
The least is one, when
they point opposite ways.

79
00:03:22,964 --> 00:03:26,743
Here is where subtraction really
matters: change in velocity.

80
00:03:27,093 --> 00:03:31,576
Aarav cruises east at six metres per
second, turns a corner, and rides

81
00:03:31,576 --> 00:03:33,150
north, still at six.

82
00:03:33,550 --> 00:03:35,328
His speed is the same.

83
00:03:35,328 --> 00:03:38,592
But change in velocity
is final minus initial.

84
00:03:38,992 --> 00:03:41,333
Flip v one and add it to v two.

85
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:45,704
The change is about eight point five
metres per second, pointing north

86
00:03:45,704 --> 00:03:46,604
west.

87
00:03:46,865 --> 00:03:47,798
Your turn.

88
00:03:47,798 --> 00:03:50,587
Is A minus B the same as B minus A?

89
00:03:50,587 --> 00:03:51,961
Pause and decide.

90
00:03:55,161 --> 00:03:56,061
No.

91
00:03:55,653 --> 00:03:58,328
Same length, but opposite directions.

92
00:03:58,328 --> 00:04:01,324
B minus A is the negative of A minus B.

93
00:04:01,974 --> 00:04:03,709
Now, one worked example.

94
00:04:04,059 --> 00:04:08,237
Forces of five newtons and three
newtons act at sixty degrees.

95
00:04:08,237 --> 00:04:09,674
Find the resultant.

96
00:04:10,174 --> 00:04:11,349
Use the rule.

97
00:04:11,349 --> 00:04:16,231
R squared equals A squared plus B
squared plus two AB cosine theta.

98
00:04:16,981 --> 00:04:20,757
Here A is five, B is three,
and cosine sixty is one half.

99
00:04:21,507 --> 00:04:24,980
So R squared is twenty five
plus nine plus fifteen.

100
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:26,451
That is forty nine.

101
00:04:27,201 --> 00:04:28,780
So R is seven newtons.

102
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:31,986
It sits between two and
eight, as the rule says.

103
00:04:32,636 --> 00:04:34,101
Now, the exam trap.

104
00:04:34,451 --> 00:04:38,373
Many students take theta as
the angle inside the triangle.

105
00:04:38,723 --> 00:04:42,744
But theta is the angle between
A and B placed tail to tail.

106
00:04:42,744 --> 00:04:46,169
Inside the triangle, it
is one eighty minus theta.

107
00:04:46,819 --> 00:04:48,274
Where is this asked?

108
00:04:48,274 --> 00:04:52,884
As short numericals: the resultant,
the angle between two vectors, or the

109
00:04:52,884 --> 00:04:54,301
size of A minus B.

110
00:04:54,901 --> 00:04:56,083
Exam level now.

111
00:04:56,083 --> 00:04:59,799
Vectors of sizes six and four
have a resultant of eight.

112
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:02,324
What is the size of their difference?

113
00:05:02,324 --> 00:05:03,556
Pause and solve.

114
00:05:08,956 --> 00:05:10,318
The answer is B.

115
00:05:10,318 --> 00:05:11,838
Two root ten units.

116
00:05:12,338 --> 00:05:17,205
Sixty four equals thirty six plus
sixteen plus two AB cosine theta.

117
00:05:17,205 --> 00:05:19,875
So two AB cosine theta is twelve.

118
00:05:20,375 --> 00:05:22,725
For the difference, the sign flips.

119
00:05:22,725 --> 00:05:24,836
Fifty two minus twelve is forty.

120
00:05:24,836 --> 00:05:26,708
Root forty is two root ten.

121
00:05:27,308 --> 00:05:28,772
Here is your recap.

122
00:05:28,772 --> 00:05:30,277
Screenshot this card.

123
00:05:33,477 --> 00:05:35,408
Can you answer these without help?

124
00:05:35,808 --> 00:05:36,708
One.

125
00:05:36,315 --> 00:05:40,346
How can three kilometres plus
four give a displacement of five?

126
00:05:41,246 --> 00:05:42,146
Two.

127
00:05:41,766 --> 00:05:45,957
What is the smallest resultant
of six newtons and eight newtons?

128
00:05:46,857 --> 00:05:47,757
Three.

129
00:05:47,445 --> 00:05:51,407
Turning a corner at a steady
speed, does your velocity change?

130
00:05:52,507 --> 00:05:56,684
Next time: what does multiplying
an arrow by minus one do?

131
00:05:56,684 --> 00:05:59,248
Multiplication of vectors by scalars.
